rhodes_render: synthetic physical-model research fixture, not a validated Rhodes
Usage: rhodes_render [--output PATH] [--seconds 0.01..60]
                     [--sample-rate 32000..192000] [--key 0..72]
                     [--velocity 0..1] [--gain 0..100] [--force]
                     [--audio-path direct|filtered|quadrature]
Writes mono 32-bit IEEE-float WAV. Key 0 maps to synthetic MIDI 28.
Existing entries are refused; --force replaces regular files only, never symlinks.
The note releases after min(1 second, 65% of duration).
Audio path defaults to direct (0 latency frames). Filtered retains its causal
48-frame FIR delay within the requested duration; no trim or tail extension.
Quadrature uses 6 fractional observations per host cell and retains 48 frames of delay.
One output unit represents one modeled volt times the explicit monitoring gain.
No normalization, clipping, measured parameters, or recorded samples are used.
